---
title: Garlic Broccoli (Suan Rong Xi Lan Hua 蒜蓉西兰花)
description: A classic and healthy Chinese side dish featuring tender-crisp broccoli florets tossed in a fragrant garlic sauce.
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 5 minutes
servings: 2
tags:
  - broccoli
  - vegetable
  - quick
  - chinese
  - side
cuisine: Chinese
course: Side
---

> Blanching the broccoli first ensures it cooks evenly and retains its vibrant green color when stir-fried.

== Prepare Ingredients ==

Cut the @broccoli{1%head} into bite-sized florets. Peel and thinly slice the tender parts of the stem if desired.
Mince the @garlic{4%cloves}.

== Blanching ==

Bring a large #pot{} of @water{1%liter} to a boil. Add @salt{1%tsp} and a drop of oil to the water.

Add the broccoli florets and blanch for ~{1.5%minutes} until they turn bright green but are still firm. Drain immediately and set aside.

== Stir-fry ==

Heat your #wok{} or large skillet over medium-high heat. Add @neutral oil{1.5%tbsp}.

Add the minced garlic and fry for ~{15%seconds} until very fragrant, taking care not to burn it.

Add the blanched broccoli back into the wok. Toss rapidly to coat with the garlic oil.

== Season and Finish ==

Season with:
- @salt{¼%tsp} (to taste)
- @sugar{¼%tsp}
- @chicken bouillon powder{½%tsp} (optional)

Toss for another ~{30%seconds} until everything is well combined and heated through. Add a splash of @water{1%tbsp} if it looks too dry.

Remove from heat and serve hot.